WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.216 --> 00:00:02.883
(people crying)

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:06.210
- [Narrator] Thousands of Palestinians,

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:07.620
nearly half of them women

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:09.840
and children have been killed and injured

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:12.450
after a week of Israeli strikes on Gaza

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:14.403
according to officials in the enclave.

00:00:15.327 --> 00:00:16.410
(airstrikes booming)

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:18.450
The attacks are Israel's response

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:20.700
to the assault by Hamas militants,

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:24.630
which killed over 1,400
Israelis on October 7th,

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:26.523
many of them women and children.

00:00:27.478 --> 00:00:31.311
(Benjamin speaking in Hebrew)

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:40.740
On Friday, Israel demanded
people in Gaza City to evacuate

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:42.780
to the southern part of the enclave,

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:45.663
prompting fears of a
humanitarian disaster.

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:50.400
But as the Israeli forces turn
parts of Gaza into rubble,

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:53.430
the question is can Palestinian civilians

00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:55.893
actually hide anywhere from the strikes?

00:00:58.110 --> 00:01:01.260
The Gaza Strip is a sliver
of land bordering Israel

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:04.830
and Egypt, twice the
size of Washington, D.C.

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:07.560
With more than two million
people living there,

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:10.729
it is one of the most densely
populated places on Earth.

00:01:10.729 --> 00:01:12.720
(airstrike booming)

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:14.580
Over the past week, nearly half

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:17.400
of the Strip's population
have fled their homes

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:20.132
according to the United Nations.

00:01:20.132 --> 00:01:24.632
(Howida speaking in foreign language)

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:31.200
People have sought shelter

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:35.040
in UN-run schools,
hospitals, and local hotels,

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:36.360
many of which have been hit

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:39.540
by Israeli bombing according to the UN.

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:42.243
But hardly anyone could flee the enclave.

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:45.030
That is because Gaza has been

00:01:45.030 --> 00:01:49.290
under blockade from both
Israel and Egypt since 2007

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:52.020
when Hamas seized to control of the area,

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:56.010
making it difficult to leave
Gaza even before the war.

00:01:56.010 --> 00:01:57.570
A heavily fortified perimeter

00:01:57.570 --> 00:02:01.050
called the Iron Wall
separates Gaza and Israel.

00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:03.240
Normally, some people
could cross the border

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:04.800
at this crossing,

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:07.680
but not since the Hamas
militants raided it.

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:10.590
The border between Egypt
and Gaza is also fortified

00:02:10.590 --> 00:02:14.730
with only one point to get
through at Rafah Crossing.

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:18.477
But Palestinians can't pass
it without a special permit

00:02:18.477 --> 00:02:19.830
(people shouting)

00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:22.950
and Israeli forces have bombed
the crossing several times

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:26.430
in recent days, making it
even more difficult to cross

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:28.200
for those who have permission,

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:30.000
according to local authorities,

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.103
Egyptian officials, and the UN.

00:02:33.390 --> 00:02:37.470
With Israel's military having
ordered a total siege on Gaza,

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:39.450
supplies of food and fuel

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:41.463
are no longer reaching the enclave.

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:46.380
Getting aid via Egypt is also
complicated by the bombing

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:48.120
of the Rafah Crossing.

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:52.080
On Tuesday, trucks purportedly
carrying aid from Egypt

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:53.490
were forced to move back

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:55.880
to the Egyptian side of the border.

00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:56.940
(airstrike booming)

00:02:56.940 --> 00:02:58.560
As densely populated areas

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:01.230
of Gaza get relentlessly bombarded,

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:04.475
hospitals are struggling
with the number of injured.

00:03:04.475 --> 00:03:09.142
(Mohammad speaking in foreign language)

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:20.070
With power running out in the Strip,

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:23.460
the hospitals are at risk
of turning into mass morgues

00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:26.790
according to the International
Committee of the Red Cross.

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:30.120
The Israeli military said
that it has a reduced capacity

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:34.110
for precision strikes because
its forces are stretched thin.

00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:36.240
Military officials haven't explained

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:38.530
why it attacked the Rafah border crossing

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:42.720
after the Israeli army
ordered Gazans to evacuate

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:44.490
to the southern part of the enclave

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:47.520
accusing Hamas of using
civilians as human shields.

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:51.240
Hamas told civilians
to stay in their homes.

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:53.430
But even as people go south,

00:03:53.430 --> 00:03:56.580
the UN warns that such
mass movement will lead

00:03:56.580 --> 00:03:59.783
to devastating humanitarian consequences.

00:03:59.783 --> 00:04:02.450
(pensive music)

